\section{Introduction}
Guibei Zhuang (zgb) is a Zhuang variety of China, within the Kra-Dai family. The search was narrow, and it found mainly audio gospel material. It found no school resources, and the codes zgb, zgn and zyb are easy to confuse. Check the code before relying on any Bible or school resource for ``Zhuang''.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school programmes specific to Guibei Zhuang were found in search.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
No grammar or dictionary specific to Guibei Zhuang was found in search.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project language page for Guibei Zhuang (reports a Bible translation as started): \url{https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/languages/zgb}
\item Joshua Project people-group page: \url{https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/people_groups/19805}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Global Recordings Network page for Guibei Zhuang: \url{https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/zgb}
\item Global Recordings Network, Luocheng recordings (filed under zgb): \url{https://globalrecordings.net/ja/language/4980}
\end{itemize}
Resources for the macrolanguage Zhuang and for Northern Zhuang (zyb) turned up but may not be Guibei. A Global Recordings page for the macrolanguage is \url{https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/zha}. The Scripture Earth page \url{https://www.scriptureearth.org/00eng.php?iso=zgn} is for a different code (zgn).

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Guibei Zhuang has many speakers, but search found no materials specific to it. Standard Zhuang is the written form in China. A curriculum would have to decide how to relate local Guibei speech to that standard, and would need local expertise.
